GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "63713160CF9B2A07"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aMissionEvents + {
    GC_Event "{9DC488BA1D796579}" {
     m_sName "Timelimit (event 6, 4200s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{A558C0EDF7C1E301}" {
      m_fDelay 4200
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{DEE7997D09F44863}" {
       m_sTitle "Timelimit reached"
       m_sMessage "GM Discretion when to end the mission"
      }
     }
    }
   }
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{2F6AA24294BA7A11}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "Mission Overview:"
     m_sContent "Unrest in the country has boiled over. Mujahideen fighters have taken over Kunar Abad by force, sending civilians fleeing from the city. With its close proximity to the Soviet FOB, the Soviet Army is forced to respond in force."\
     ""\
     "Soviet objective: Clear the city of enemy combatants and blow up any ammo storage crates found"\
     "MUJ Objective: Fight along AI blocking the Soviet force from moving through the city"\
     ""\
     "This Mission does not have any hard end conditions. GM´s discretion (see mission notes)"\
     ""
    }
    GC_Briefing "{23E7C449E5A6A11D}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "Enemy"
     m_sContent "Mujahideen forces located within Kunar Abad, estimated Company (+) strength (approx. 80-120 fighters). Armed with AK-pattern rifles, machine guns, and limited anti-tank weapons. Dressed in civilian clothing. Civilian hostages held at the market."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{CFB6303ECD113914}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "ENEMY"
     m_sContent "Soviet forces have established a military base to the east of our position. The Soviets operate with mechanised infantry, equipped with AK-74 rifles, machine guns, grenade launchers, and armoured vehicles including BTR-70 APCs. They have access to substantial ammunition and medical supplies."\
     ""\
     "The Soviets wear khaki uniforms and are well-trained soldiers. They will likely conduct a clearing operation through Kunar Abad once they realise we have taken the town. Expect them to move systematically, building by building, and they will not hesitate to use their superior firepower."\
     ""\
     "WARNING: Soviet snipers have been observed in the hills surrounding the city. Many brothers have already been killed trying to move through open ground outside the city limits. DO NOT leave the city - stay within the buildings and streets where their snipers cannot easily target you. The hills are a death trap."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{365BB10BBEAF114A}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "Orders"
     m_sContent "200 Company is to clear Kunar Abad and eliminate Mujahideen forces. Destroy any enemy ammunition caches found. Establish blocking position to the west."\
     ""\
     "RESTRICT USE OF ANTI-TANK WEAPONS AND EXPLOSIVES - civilian population remains in the area."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{211B19DD20C498E3}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "FRIENDLY FORCES"
     m_sContent "Our main force consists of approximately 250-300 fighters spread throughout Kunar Abad. Many brothers are positioned in defensive positions around key buildings and intersections. A group of civilian hostages are being held at the market near grid 0308-0275 - they are leverage and must be protected."\
     ""\
     "Another platoon has been assigned to guard the ammunition cache at the compound in grid 0324-0261."\
     ""\
     "Our transport buses that brought us from Asadabad and the Shuryak Valley have been positioned as roadblocks on the western approaches to deny the Soviets easy entry."\
     ""\
     "Note: AI will be spawned in as Soviets move through the city."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{4E9EDA3C158F25D8}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "Signals"
     m_sContent "Company Net - 42MHz"\
     ""\
     "Only CO, Coy Sgt, PLs, and BTR crews have radios."\
     ""\
     "Callsigns:"\
     "200 - Company HQ"\
     "201 - 1st Platoon HQ (with BTRs)"\
     "201, 202, 203 - 1st Platoon Squads"\
     "204 - 2nd Platoon HQ"\
     "204, 205, 206 - 2nd Platoon Squads"\
     "207 - 3rd Platoon HQ"\
     "207, 208, 209 - 3rd Platoon Squads"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{EDD1A5400A72FF7A}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "MISSION"
     m_sContent "Our platoon, along with our brother fighters throughout the city, will defend Kunar Abad and the ammunition cache for as long as possible. This position is critical - we are establishing a staging point for our planned assault on the Soviet FOB. Every hour we hold this ground gives our commanders time to prepare the offensive."\
     ""\
     "The ammunition cache hidden in the city must not fall into Soviet hands."\
     ""\
     "Mission makers note: DO NOT CHANGE WEAPONS unless you run out of ammo. Do not kill AIs to take their weapons."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F083045432D9B90E}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "Transport"
     m_sContent "3x BTR-70s (assigned to 1st Platoon)"\
     "1x Transport Truck with extra supplies and explosives"\
     ""\
     ""\
     "Note: Don’t expect to be able to push wrecks/busses out of the way."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{24F1EAC177B04A0D}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "TASKS AND ORDERS"
     m_sContent "Your platoon is organised as:"\
     "- Racek-21: First fighter section"\
     "- Racek-22: Second fighter section"\
     "- Racek-23: Third fighter section"\
     ""\
     "Your responsibilities:"\
     "a) Defend Kunar Abad - STAY WITHIN THE CITY LIMITS"\
     "b) Maintain observation on Soviet movements and report via the radioman"\
     "c) Coordinate with other fighter groups in the city when possible"\
     "d) Use the urban terrain to your advantage - buildings provide cover and ambush positions"\
     "e) Preserve fighter strength - withdraw and reposition when faced with overwhelming force rather than dying needlessly"\
     "f) DO NOT attempt to move into the hills - Soviet snipers will kill you"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{D25C6E1420641D51}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "SUPPORT"\
     ""
     m_sContent "We have no vehicle support. The buses cannot move from their blocking positions. No artillery or air support is available."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{DB5AA4E58E49DCD2}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "COMMAND AND SIGNALS"
     m_sContent "Only the radioman carries a radio (R-148). All communication with other sections must be through runners or face-to-face contact. Conserve radio batteries - only critical information should be transmitted."\
     ""\
     "Radio Net: 50.00MHz - Main Command Net"\
     ""\
     "Command"\
     "Overall command for the defence of Kunar Abad rests with the commanders at the ammunition cache compound (grid 0324-0261). Your section leaders will direct local tactics in your assigned sectors."\
     ""\
     "Chain of command:"\
     "- Section Leader (Racek-21)"\
     "- 1st Fighter Section (Racek-22)"\
     "- 2nd Fighter Section (Racek-22)"\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{113FB248A8C0D8AB}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "WEATHER"
     m_sContent "Date: 2001/08/01"\
     "Time Now: 0700h (first light)"\
     "Weather: Clear and sunny with light haze"\
     "Visibility: Good, approximately 2000 metres"\
     "Temperature: Hot - conserve water"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{C604817D81762D7D}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "FINAL GUIDANCE"
     m_sContent "Brothers, we fight for our land and our future. The Soviets have superior equipment and training, but we have determination and knowledge of this ground. Use the buildings, use the narrow streets, make them pay for every metre. When they come in strength, fall back and regroup - live to fight again."\
     ""\
     "The hostages at the market are valuable. Do not let the Soviets rescue them easily."\
     ""\
     "REMEMBER: Stay in the city. The hills belong to their snipers. Many good fighters have died learning this lesson - do not be the next."\
     ""\
     "Allah is with us. Fight with courage and cunning."\
     ""
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "GC_MUJ"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{7985330694CCF0D8}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "VI. Mission notes:"
     m_sContent "<h2>Mission Intent</h2>"\
     "- Soviet Force is expected to clear through every building in Kunar Abad. If Ammo Caches are located they are to be blown up."\
     "- MUJ Force is expected to survive for as long as possible causing problems for the Soviet Force."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Setup timer</h2>"\
     "None"\
     ""\
     "<h2>JIP Teleport</h2>"\
     "Enabled for 5 min. After that - walk to friendlies"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Soviet Victory</h2>"\
     "Major Victory"\
     "1x Ammo cache destroyed"\
     "Company in blocking position towards Shan Kalay (034-025 and 034-026)"\
     ""\
     "Minor Victory"\
     "Company in blocking position towards Shan Kalay (034-025 and 034-026) but unable to locate the Ammo cache"\
     ""\
     "<h2>Soviet Defeat</h2>"\
     "90% casualties. A mesage will appear and GM is expected to call the mission if Soviets are unable to accomplish the mission."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Timelimit of 70 min. A message will appear and GM can call</h2>"\
     ""\
     "GM is expected to call the mission. But should allow for firefights to end."\
     ""\
     "<h2>Game Mastering</h2>"\
     "AI may get stuck near buildings; Game Masters are authorized to reposition or spawn additional AI if the mission becomes too easy for the players."\
     ""\
     "Maintain balance and challenge, but ensure the mission remains fair and engaging."\
     ""\
     ""\
     "<h2>Mission by Perfk</h2>"\
     "Last updated: 2026-01-16"\
     ""
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
